        "id": "p15-q21-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the angle of elevation of $Q$ from $O$, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q21-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "33.35^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q21-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Find OA using tangent, OB using the sine rule, then the elevation using tangent.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In $\\triangle OAP$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan37^\\circ&=\\frac{300}{OA}\\\\OA&=\\frac{300}{\\tan37^\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\nIn the ground triangle:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle AOB&=180^\\circ-50^\\circ-42^\\circ\\\\\\angle AOB&=88^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the sine rule in $\\triangle OAB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{OB}{\\sin50^\\circ}&=\\frac{OA}{\\sin42^\\circ}\\\\OB&=\\frac{300\\sin50^\\circ}{\\tan37^\\circ\\sin42^\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\nLet the angle of elevation of $Q$ from $O$ be $\\phi$. Since $QB=300\\text{ m}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\phi&=\\frac{300}{OB}\\\\\\phi&=\\tan^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\tan37^\\circ\\sin42^\\circ}{\\sin50^\\circ}\\right)\\\\\\phi&\\approx33.35^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 122
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q21-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the distance the helicopter flew from $P$ to $Q$, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
