        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q21-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "594.61\\text{ m}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q21-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the sine rule to find AB; the equal flight heights give PQ = AB.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Using $OA=\\dfrac{300}{\\tan37^\\circ}$ from part (a), in $\\triangle OAB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle AOB&=180^\\circ-50^\\circ-42^\\circ\\\\\\angle AOB&=88^\\circ\\\\\\frac{AB}{\\sin88^\\circ}&=\\frac{OA}{\\sin42^\\circ}\\\\AB&=\\frac{300\\sin88^\\circ}{\\tan37^\\circ\\sin42^\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe helicopter maintains the same vertical height, so its flight distance equals the ground separation:\n$$\\begin{align*}PQ&=AB\\\\PQ&\\approx594.61\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 96
      }
    ]
